Export the per-node score vector main.py already computes.

main.py builds `scores`, measures auc_roc and auc_prc on it, prints both and
discards the vector. GraFlag publishes the scores a method computed rather
than a number it printed.

Written behind GRAFLAG_SCORE_OUT so the patched file behaves exactly as
upstream when the variable is unset: the repository's own README commands
produce byte-identical output to the unpatched tree.

The labels are written beside the scores because `ano_label` comes from
upstream's own load_mat, and pairing the published scores against a label
column read separately would depend on both agreeing about node order.

Note main.py has CRLF line terminators; this patch preserves them. Rewriting
the file with LF would have turned a three-line change into a 169-line diff
that breaks on any upstream edit.

Generated with `git diff` against the tree SOURCE_REF pins.

diff --git a/main.py b/main.py
index e79bd75..0c61be0 100644
--- a/main.py
+++ b/main.py
@@ -160,6 +160,9 @@ with warnings.catch_warnings():
         scores = -scores.detach().cpu().numpy()
         auc_roc = roc_auc_score(ano_label, scores)
         auc_prc = prc_auc_score(ano_label, scores)
+        if os.environ.get('GRAFLAG_SCORE_OUT'):
+            np.savetxt(os.environ['GRAFLAG_SCORE_OUT'], scores)
+            np.savetxt(os.environ['GRAFLAG_SCORE_OUT'] + '.label', np.asarray(ano_label))
     time_eval_end = datetime.datetime.now()
     timedelta_eval = time_eval_end - time_eval_start
 if args.print_results:
